    <section class="sql-sheet-section">
        <div class="sql-section-heading">
            <span class="sql-section-number">1</span>
            <div>
                <h2>Count the Groups</h2>
                <p>Start with row counts so you can see how the data is distributed.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <details class="sql-syntax-ref">
            <summary><i class="fa-solid fa-code"></i> Reference pattern — COUNT and GROUP BY</summary>
            <div class="sql-syntax-body">
                <pre><code>-- Count rows in each group
SELECT group_column, COUNT(*) AS row_count
FROM table_name
GROUP BY group_column;

-- Count after a join
SELECT category_column, COUNT(*) AS row_count
FROM first_table AS a
INNER JOIN second_table AS b
    ON a.primary_key = b.foreign_key
GROUP BY category_column
ORDER BY row_count DESC;</code></pre>
                <p><code>GROUP BY</code> creates one summary row per group. <code>COUNT(*)</code> tells you how many source rows ended up in each summary.</p>
            </div>
        </details>

