    <section class="sql-sheet-section">
        <div class="sql-section-heading">
            <span class="sql-section-number">2</span>
            <div>
                <h2>Average, Total, Highest, and Lowest</h2>
                <p>Move from raw counts into richer summary measures.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <details class="sql-syntax-ref">
            <summary><i class="fa-solid fa-code"></i> Reference pattern — AVG, SUM, MAX, MIN</summary>
            <div class="sql-syntax-body">
                <pre><code>-- Average a numeric value in each group
SELECT group_column, AVG(number_column) AS average_value
FROM table_name
GROUP BY group_column;

-- Add up a numeric value in each group
SELECT group_column, SUM(number_column) AS total_value
FROM table_name
GROUP BY group_column;

-- Find the largest and smallest value in each group
SELECT group_column,
       MAX(number_column) AS highest_value,
       MIN(number_column) AS lowest_value
FROM table_name
GROUP BY group_column;</code></pre>
                <p>Aggregate functions collapse many rows into one summary. Choose the grouping column first, then decide which measure helps answer the reporting question.</p>
            </div>
        </details>

