    <section class="sql-sheet-section">
        <div class="sql-section-heading">
            <span class="sql-section-number">3</span>
            <div>
                <h2>Filter Groups with HAVING</h2>
                <p>Now add thresholds to the grouped results.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <details class="sql-syntax-ref">
            <summary><i class="fa-solid fa-code"></i> Reference pattern — HAVING after aggregation</summary>
            <div class="sql-syntax-body">
                <pre><code>-- Keep only the groups that meet a threshold
SELECT group_column, COUNT(*) AS row_count
FROM table_name
GROUP BY group_column
HAVING COUNT(*) >= 4;

-- HAVING can also test averages or totals
SELECT group_column, AVG(score_column) AS average_score
FROM table_name
GROUP BY group_column
HAVING AVG(score_column) > 85
ORDER BY average_score DESC;</code></pre>
                <p><code>HAVING</code> is for group-level conditions. If the condition is about the summary, it belongs after <code>GROUP BY</code>, not in <code>WHERE</code>.</p>
            </div>
        </details>

